      "title": "Broken Function Level Authorization via Client-Supplied Header on /admin",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "The `/admin` endpoint relies solely on a client-supplied HTTP header (`x-admin`) to authorize administrative access. An unauthenticated attacker can supply `x-admin: 1` to bypass authorization checks and access the restricted admin panel.",
      "poc": "1. Send a GET request to `/admin` without headers and observe a 403 Forbidden response.\n2. Send a GET request to `/admin` with the header `x-admin: 1` and observe a 200 OK response with administrative panel content.",
      "target": "/workspace/test-vuln-node",
      "endpoint": "/admin",
      "method": "GET",
      "cvss": 5.3,
      "finding_class": "dynamic",
      "source": "/opt/ares/strix/strix_runs/test-vuln-node_3ce7/vulnerabilities.json"
    },
    {
      "title": "SQL Injection in /item endpoint",
      "severity": "critical",
      "description": "The `/item` endpoint uses f-string interpolation to construct SQL queries, allowing attackers to inject arbitrary SQL via the `id` parameter.",
      "poc": "1. Send a request to `/item` with a valid ID to establish a baseline.\n2. Send a request with `id=1%20AND%201=1` to confirm boolean-based injection.\n3. Send a request with `id=1%20AND%201=2` to confirm the negative case.\n4. Use a `UNION SELECT` payload to extract arbitrary data.",
      "target": "/workspace/test-vuln-node",
      "endpoint": "/item",
      "method": "GET",
      "cvss": 9.1,
      "finding_class": "dynamic",
      "source": "/opt/ares/strix/strix_runs/test-vuln-node_3ce7/vulnerabilities.json"
    },
